Aggregate Window Functions
Used to calculate running totals, moving averages, or cumulative statistics across a “window” of rows — without collapsing them into one row

| Need                                          | Use               |
| --------------------------------------------- | ----------------- |
| To track a **running total (cumulative sum)** | `SUM()`           |
| To find a **moving or cumulative average**    | `AVG()`           |
| To count **how many rows processed so far**   | `COUNT()`         |
| To check **smallest or largest value so far** | `MIN()` / `MAX()` |



| Function    | One-liner                                                            | Example Query                                                                                                                            |
| ----------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **SUM()**   | Calculates a **running or cumulative total** across rows.            | `sql SELECT name, department, salary, SUM(salary) OVER (PARTITION BY department ORDER BY salary) AS running_total FROM employee_bonus; ` |
| **AVG()**   | Calculates a **moving or cumulative average** within each partition. | `sql SELECT name, department, salary, AVG(salary) OVER (PARTITION BY department ORDER BY salary) AS running_avg FROM employee_bonus; `   |
| **COUNT()** | Shows a **running count** of rows up to the current one.             | `sql SELECT name, department, COUNT(*) OVER (PARTITION BY department ORDER BY salary) AS running_count FROM employee_bonus; `            |
| **MIN()**   | Returns the **minimum value seen so far** in the ordered window.     | `sql SELECT name, department, salary, MIN(salary) OVER (PARTITION BY department ORDER BY salary) AS min_so_far FROM employee_bonus; `    |
| **MAX()**   | Returns the **maximum value seen so far** in the ordered window.     | `sql SELECT name, department, salary, MAX(salary) OVER (PARTITION BY department ORDER BY salary) AS max_so_far FROM employee_bonus; `    |


Add a window frame for more control
ROWS BETWEEN UNBOUNDED PRECEDING AND CURRENT ROW -->“from the first row in this partition up to the current one.”
